WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.930
Even as one of only a handful of female leads
to carry a multi-million-dollar film franchise,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:10.970
Kate Beckinsale still feels unknown or at
the very least unappreciated.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:14.940
Beckinsale is clearly capable of delivering
exceptional work, but in spite of what she's

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:20.009
proven she can do with the right script, opportunities
to display her dramatic chops have come far

00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:21.510
too infrequently.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.300
Here are a few possible reasons why Hollywood
isn't offering Kate Beckinsale more opportunities

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.909
to shine.

00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:32.660
Pearl Harbor was a flop
Beckinsale's potential big break for American

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:35.719
audiences ended up a complete disaster.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:41.039
After a standout performance alongside Claire
Danes in 1999's Brokedown Palace, Beckinsale

00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:43.670
was poised to really bust out as a leading
woman.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:48.859
But the 2001 period blockbuster Pearl Harbor,
which saw Beckinsale playing the love interest

00:00:48.859 --> 00:00:53.079
to both Ben Affleck and Josh Hartnett, was
almost unanimously panned.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:57.670
Had the film succeeded, or had Beckinsale's
performance outshined the production itself,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:02.640
her career likely would have taken a different
path one leading to more high-profile, dramatic

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.640
roles.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.480
To make matters worse, after Pearl Harbor
stunted Beckinsale's growth as a viable lead

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.160
in a big-budget drama, her next film all but
stopped her chances of working in the romantic

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.320
comedy genre.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:20.260
No serendipity here
The 2001 romcom Serendipity starring Beckinsale

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:23.770
and John Cusack fell flat with critics as
well as the general public.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:30.180
By that point, audiences had suffered through
or supported nearly two decades of adorable-yet-hapless

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:35.640
John Cusack characters, and by the turn of
the century, the magic had started to wear

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.640
thin.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.700
This is not to say either star was particularly
to blame for the film's ultimate failure.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:44.600
Had Serendipity been better, it might have
been a perfect pivot for Beckinsale.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.280
Alas, it was not to be.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.510
"I have to give it all up now, don't I?"

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:57.730
Married to Underworld
After she was tapped to play Selene in 2003's

00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:01.060
Underworld, Beckinsale hit it off with director
Len Wiseman.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.180
The two became romantic, and were married
within two years.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.860
Now more than a decade later, Wiseman and
Beckinsale have worked on multiple films together,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.330
including several in the Underworld franchise,
before their split in 2016.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.130
The Underworld films in particular cost relatively
little to produce, do well at the box office

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:22.380
and have been quite profitable, but they aren't
exactly considered great cinema.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:26.450
So while the franchise has been rolling along,
Beckinsale's career has suffered.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:30.890
Amongst audiences, directors, and casting
agents, she may be too closely associated

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.930
with Selene from Underworld for them imagine
her in any other role.

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:39.220
"Imprisonment for all time."

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.700
Ageism
Unfortunately, Beckinsale is in a kind of

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:47.610
acting purgatory simultaneously too old and
too young to snatch up the most desirable

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.819
roles in the industry.

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:53.569
While male leads can work well into their
50s and 60s, female leads are more often than

00:02:53.569 --> 00:02:56.210
not left out of roles once they pass 40.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:01.819
As it stands, Beckinsale had only one credit
in 2017, a drama called The Only Living Boy

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:07.280
in New York alongside Pierce Brosnan, Jeff
Bridges, Cynthia Nixon, and Callum Turner.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.500
In the movie, Beckinsale's character plays
a mistress who begins an affair with her lover's

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.500
son.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.290
Working with established talent and rising
stars can only be good for Beckinsale's continued

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.270
success in Hollywood, but this doesn't change
the fact that she was chosen for her role

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.870
precisely because of her age and her looks.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.870
"Is that kind of vulgarity really necessary?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.450
"What kind of vulgarity would you prefer?"

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.260
Sexism
In 2016, Beckinsale appeared on The Graham

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.610
Norton Show and revealed some disparaging
jabs director Michael Bay made at her while

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.980
he was on the press junket for Pearl Harbor.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.380
She said:
"When we were promoting the film, Michael

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.400
was asked why he had chosen Ben [Affleck]
and Josh [Hartnett], and he said, 'I have

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.450
worked with Ben before and I love him, and
Josh is so manly and a wonderful actor.'"

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:52.390
But Bay apparently didn't share the same thoughts
about Beckinsale's ability.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.110
She continued:
"Then when he was asked about me, he'd say,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.970
'Kate wasn't so attractive that she would
alienate the female audience.'"

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:05.830
In a 2001 interview with Movieline, Bay confirmed
his sentiments, saying of why he cast Beckinsale:

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.319
"I didn't want someone who was too beautiful.

00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:11.190
Women feel disturbed when they see someone's
too pretty."

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:16.269
Regardless of what Bay thinks of her appearance,
Beckinsale has frequently been typecast for

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:18.099
her good looks and physique.

00:04:18.099 --> 00:04:19.729
It's a double edged sword.

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:25.210
Whether in recent horror films like The Disappointments
Room or Stonehearst Asylum, or action flicks

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:29.759
such as Total Recall or the Underworld series,
she's not exactly doing Shakespeare in the

00:04:29.759 --> 00:04:30.759
park.

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:35.660
Having played so many of these types of characters
over the past 20-plus years, it's easy to

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.770
see how she's been overlooked for... well...

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.770
everything else.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:42.400
"You like it?"

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.400
"Yeah, it's funny."

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:49.139
A turn to TV
The average cost to produce and market a wide-release

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:53.860
film has skyrocketed over the last 30 years,
and studios are no longer willing to take

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:58.559
risks on small-budget indies or period dramas
without major star power.

00:04:58.559 --> 00:05:02.660
Unfortunately, these are precisely the types
of films in which Beckinsale has excelled.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:07.180
With the big screen less hospitable than ever,
it's unsurprising that Beckinsale turned to

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.180
TV.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:13.120
In 2018, she was announced as the star of
the limited-run Amazon series The Widow, about

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:17.659
a woman drawn into a dangerous quest after
spotting her supposedly late husband on the

00:05:17.659 --> 00:05:18.659
news.

00:05:18.659 --> 00:05:23.210
Clearly, an actress of Beckinsale's talent
and diverse résumé is always just the right

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.129
script away from a comeback.

00:05:25.129 --> 00:05:26.610
Time will tell if this is it.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:27.960
Thanks for watching!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.059
